Subject: [PATCH] console: pick the socket family from the address in _verify_port

nova/console/serial.py:_verify_port() probes a candidate TCP port with a
bare socket.socket(), which defaults to AF_INET, then binds
[serial_console] proxyclient_address to it. On an IPv6-only deployment
that address is an IPv6 literal, and binding an IPv6 address to an
AF_INET socket always raises, so every port in serial_console.port_range
looks occupied:

    nova.exception.SocketPortRangeExhaustedException: Not able to acquire
    a free port for 2602:f86e:140:120:1021:14ff:fef2:4b4f

acquire_port() walks the whole range, treats all ~10000 ports as in use,
and raises. That propagates out of _create_serial_consoles() in the
libvirt driver, so the guest never builds: the instance goes to ERROR and
no domain is left on the hypervisor. It is not specific to one instance -
with [serial_console] enabled = true, NO instance can boot on an
IPv6-only cloud.

There is no configuration-only workaround. proxyclient_address is derived
from the compute's api_interface address, and on this estate every node's
API interface is IPv6-only - the control node has no IPv4 address at all -
so there is no v4 address to fall back to and no port_range that helps.

Choose the address family from the host string instead.

Applied against the installed copy in the venv, because the nova-base
Dockerfile runs kolla_patch after `pip install /nova`. Path uses the
version-independent `python3` symlink created in
docker/openstack-base/Dockerfile.j2.

--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/nova/console/serial.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/nova/console/serial.py
@@ -80,7 +80,12 @@
 
 
 def _verify_port(host, port):
-    s = socket.socket()
+    # socket.socket() defaults to AF_INET. Binding an IPv6 literal to an
+    # AF_INET socket always raises, which would make every port in
+    # serial_console.port_range look occupied and defeat acquire_port().
+    # Derive the family from the address so IPv6-only deployments work.
+    family = socket.AF_INET6 if ':' in host else socket.AF_INET
+    s = socket.socket(family)
     try:
         s.bind((host, port))
     except socket.error as e:
